WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:03.240
- There's millions of dollars
inside these envelopes.

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.950
- [Narrator] Meet Josh Fox.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.290
- If you wanna change your life,

00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:09.090
this is the conversation for you.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:11.790
You can make $6.3 million.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.980
We love money.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.360
- [Narrator] In the past few years,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.130
Fox has built an empire,

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.600
recently with some assistance

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.700
from "Shark Tank" investor Kevin O'Leary

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.480
by taking advantage of an
obscure pandemic era tax break.

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.640
- The Employee Retention Credit Program.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:28.283
Do you even know what that is?

00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:30.780
- This is the modern-day gold rush.

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:31.860
That's what I'm calling it.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:33.450
- Oh, this is a total gold rush.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.120
- [Narrator] Since 2021, Fox's firm,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.860
Bottom Line Concepts, has worked

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.680
with thousands of small
businesses and nonprofits

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.760
in an effort to pursue more
than $6 billion in tax breaks,

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.080
which could yield Bottom Line
more than $1 billion in fees.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:50.070
- We're rich.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:53.220
- [Narrator] But is this gold
rush too good to be true?

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.320
- One of the things we've seen

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:58.770
with these pandemic programs
is when you do things

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:03.733
in a hurry, you have
unintended consequences.

00:01:03.733 --> 00:01:05.010
(pensive music)

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.600
- [Narrator] In March of 2020,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.930
as the coronavirus pandemic
first gripped the country,

00:01:09.930 --> 00:01:13.770
President Trump signed
the $2 trillion CARES Act.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.200
- I've never signed
anything with a T on it.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.120
- [Narrator] The largest
economic stimulus package

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.440
in US history.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:22.080
One of the lesser known
parts of that legislation

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.590
was the employee retention
tax credit or ERC.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:27.180
- There was real concern
during the pandemic

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:29.340
that people would get
laid off and lose some

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:31.590
of that attachment to
a particular employer

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:34.620
and it'd be harder to turn
the economy back on again.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.720
The real core point of this credit

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.660
was to keep workers
attached to their jobs.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.580
- [Narrator] To qualify for the ERC,

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.910
a business or nonprofit
must meet certain criteria.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:47.040
- To get in, you have to
meet one of two tests,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.380
either your revenue had to
drop by a specific amount.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.720
The other way is you had
to have a government order

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.240
that was fully or partially
suspending your business.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:56.430
- [Narrator] The amount of
a business can qualify for

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.860
depends on its number of employees

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.260
and which quarters the
business was affected

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:02.610
during the pandemic.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:04.800
- The number you'll see really frequently

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.530
in all the ads is 26,000 per employee.

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:09.450
- See if your company qualifies

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:12.420
for up to $26,000 per employee.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:15.840
- And I think that's basically
5,000 per employee in 2020,

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:17.700
which was the limit, and then 7,000

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.790
for each of the first
three quarters in 2021,

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:22.110
which was the limit for that year.

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:25.140
So you'll see this 26,000
per employee number.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.210
That's the maximum you could qualify for

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.090
if you were eligible for
all of those quarters.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.360
- [Narrator] Determining if a
business qualifies for the ERC

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.550
and for how much isn't straightforward.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.100
It's also a challenge for the IRS.

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:39.480
- The employee retention credit

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:44.190
is an extremely complicated
filing to process.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:45.060
- [Narrator] That's where firms

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.920
like Bottom Line Concepts come in.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:48.870
- So I've got the expert with me.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.220
This is Josh Fox.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.070
- [Narrator] Although the
ERC expired in late 2021,

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:56.430
the window to claim the credit
retroactively remains open

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.320
until early 2025.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.210
- I want you to get this money.

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.430
You'd be crazy not to get this.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.320
- [Narrator] To find eligible businesses,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.937
firms like Bottom Line
are advertising heavily.

00:03:06.937 --> 00:03:08.790
- "What's the ERC?" you ask.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:11.040
- [Narrator] Shark Tank
veteran Kevin O'Leary

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.020
is Bottom Line's best known partner.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:14.940
- What is this?

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:19.170
- This is hundreds of millions
of dollars, literally, Kevin.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:21.240
- [Narrator] O'Leary told
The Wall Street Journal

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.400
why he joined Forces with Bottom Line.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:26.310
- I said, "Look, I need to
buy a piece of the company.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:27.900
I need to be a shareholder."

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.490
But in this case, it made no sense

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:32.940
'cause this program's going
away in a matter of months.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.160
So I said, "Let's form a new entity.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.360
Let's be partners in it.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.220
We're gonna call it WonderTrust."

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:39.780
- [Narrator] WonderTrust is a website

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.370
that connects potential businesses

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:42.660
with Bottom Line.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:43.920
- I will get behind this.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.570
I'll go all over network television,

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:49.350
all over social and tell
people about this program

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.670
'cause I'm a believer in it

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:52.980
and I'll put my own companies through it.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.480
So I'll eat my own cooking.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.480
Mr. Wonderful here, and
there's no debate about this.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.820
- [Narrator] WonderTrust
said it has submitted

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.980
about $140 million

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:06.420
in ERC claims for more than 780 employers.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:08.780
- I'm pounding the table. I'm telling...

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.060
Most small businesses know who I am

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:15.060
and I'm telling them this
is mandate number one.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.900
You have months left to look
into this and you should.

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:19.770
- [Narrator] For the businesses

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:23.190
that are unconvinced or
unreceptive to commercials,

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:26.010
Bottom Line has also
created a referral network

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:27.720
of about 50,000 people.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:29.820
- These are people who are
not on salary at Bottom Line.

00:04:29.820 --> 00:04:31.050
They may have another job.

00:04:31.050 --> 00:04:34.080
They may be semi-retired,
they may be fully retired

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.370
and they're just out there talking

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:37.470
to every employer they can find.

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:40.350
- What else are the
people on this call doing?

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:42.600
There's 600 people today on the call

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:45.570
that you can make $6.3 million.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.220
- [Narrator] One of the tools Bottom Line

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:50.310
has used to recruit potential
affiliates is online video.

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:51.150
- One of the videos

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.360
is called "Become a
Millionaire with Bottom Line."

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.420
- So 100 clients divided by 24 months,

00:04:57.420 --> 00:05:02.070
you have to bring us four clients a month.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:05.010
- They run through the
math, "Bring me these number

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:09.510
of people and look how
much money you can make."

00:05:09.510 --> 00:05:14.040
- So one client a week for
two years, you make 1,300,000.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:15.750
- We're making millionaires.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:17.940
This is easy money.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.190
It's a way to get rich.

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:21.360
- Carrie Hagen-Smith

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:23.790
is a Bottom Line Concepts
referral partner.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:24.990
Hagen-Smith is working

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:27.780
with 24 clients that
she expects will receive

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:31.500
about $1.4 million back from the IRS.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:34.110
- They have not all gotten
their paperwork in yet,

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:37.290
so it's a very long process,
both on the client side

00:05:37.290 --> 00:05:39.930
and on Bottom Line Concept side.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.120
And then we add the third element,

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:44.280
which is the IRS processing.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:46.410
- [Narrator] Hagen-Smith said her success

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:49.590
has come primarily from
face-to-face interactions.

00:05:49.590 --> 00:05:51.780
- My biggest strategy has been

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.510
with a partner and we go bold calling.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:57.360
That's not wimping out and
cold calling on the phone.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.230
That's walking boldfaced
into the business's door

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:04.050
and actually being the local face

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:08.040
that they can rely on for ERC Answers.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:10.320
- [Narrator] Bottom Line
doesn't require its customers

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:11.670
to shell out cash.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:15.930
Instead, everyone gets paid
once the IRS issues a check.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:17.940
- You don't have to buy anything.

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.670
You don't have to spend
a lot of money upfront.

00:06:20.670 --> 00:06:22.530
You don't have to convince your clients

00:06:22.530 --> 00:06:23.880
to write you a check.

00:06:23.880 --> 00:06:27.210
You get money at the end
once everyone is happy

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:30.090
and you're helping small
businesses along the way.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.260
That's the pitch.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.120
- Everything we do, we're doing

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.620
because you've signed a contract

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.190
and you're going to get the
actual check back from the IRS.

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:39.030
That's it.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:42.030
That alleviates a lot of
those fears that people have

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.010
from hearing the scam alerts.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.050
- I actually started digging into it

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:50.700
and looked at people that could
process these applications.

00:06:50.700 --> 00:06:52.470
I came to the conclusion,
there's a lot of, well,

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.080
for lack of a better word,
schlockers out there.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.540
- [Narrator] Despite
his support for the ERC,

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.650
O'Leary acknowledges

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.110
that there are some
unscrupulous firms involved

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:02.460
in the ERC space.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.400
- I think anybody that
takes a payment upfront,

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.820
I would not use them because
why are they doing that?

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.280
- [Narrator] Every year as the
nation heads into tax season,

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:14.880
the IRS releases a list of
the most common tax scams

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.980
for taxpayers to be mindful of.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:21.810
At the top of that list for
2023 was fraudulent ERC claims.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:26.810
- For the IRS, the ERC
is a giant headache.

00:07:27.330 --> 00:07:29.550
On the one hand, what's happened

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:33.360
is because they've gotten
so many applications,

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:34.980
there've been a lot of complaints

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:38.880
that they haven't processed
these refunds quickly enough.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:42.270
And I've talked to small
businesses who need the money

00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:45.780
who really feel they
qualify and they haven't

00:07:45.780 --> 00:07:47.070
and they've been waiting.

00:07:47.070 --> 00:07:51.720
On the other hand, the IRS is
really worried about fraud.

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:54.420
- Figuring out whether what's legal here

00:07:54.420 --> 00:07:55.920
and what's not is is really tricky.

00:07:55.920 --> 00:07:58.530
I think we're very much in
the early stages of that.

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.300
You know, the IRS has certainly indicated

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.610
that it thinks it is seeing,

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:05.730
and the IRS does not name
particular firms in this,

00:08:05.730 --> 00:08:06.563
but they've indicated

00:08:06.563 --> 00:08:09.240
that they're seeing what they
think are a significant number

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:13.560
of fraudulent or overstated
or ineligible claims.

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:15.360
- [Narrator] In a statement
to The Wall Street Journal,

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.820
Bottom Line wrote, "We are
proud of the company's record

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.610
of delivering valuable
services to American businesses

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:23.790
with no upfront fees in a
compliant and transparent manner,

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:27.150
including educating small
businesses on the ERC program

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.400
and helping them reinvest
in their business

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.510
and their workforce

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.270
to the benefit of local
communities across the country.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:36.393
- Look at all these checks I
am actually holding in my hand.

